  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malala Fund for Girls&apos; Right to Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Malala Fund for Girls&apos; Right to Education was established on 10 December 2012 and enables the implementation of projects, especially in post-conflict and post-disaster countries, addressing key areas of concern relating to girls&apos; education. Interventions will aim to widen access to education and all learning opportunities, improve the retention and completion rates of girls by enhancing the quality of education so that it is gender-transformative and meets girls&apos; and women&apos;s needs. Special attention will be given to eliminating discrimination against girls in the learning process. The Fund is a multi-donor special account.</narrative>
  </description>
